        "text": "Importantly, we actually look for non crypto experience. So, for example, if you're a technologist, you have a programmer, good programming skills. The crypto aspect is relatively easy to learn, actually, if you're a marketing person, if you're a community manager, if you're a legal person. So we look for those core skills that you already have in other industries. Crypto, whether you know it or not, takes a little bit of time to learn, but it's actually not that difficult. So any kind of relevant crypto experience is okay. We don't require you to work in a different exchange, we don't require you to run a crypto project yourself before. But some level of crypto exposure is helpful. And also the fact that if you believe in the crypto mission, that's very helpful. So let's talk about experience, more about belief.",
